  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "WFG-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-weierstrass-formal-group",
      "title": "The integral Weierstrass formal group law and its invariant logarithm",
      "hypotheses": "An arbitrary commutative ring R and a Weierstrass equation W with coefficients a₁, a₂, a₃, a₄, a₆∈R; for the formal logarithm and analytic coordinate comparison, a field K of characteristic zero; for the unit-ball and short-model specialization, a characteristic-zero ultrametric valued field K with closed unit ball R containing the coefficients of W (namely |g₂|≤1, |g₃|≤1, and |2|=1 on y²=x³−(g₂/4)x−g₃/4).",
      "statement": "A contractive fixed-point equation in local coordinates T=−x/y, w=−1/y defines a unique series w_W(T)=T³w_U(T)∈R[[T]] with w_U(0)=1, together with division-free secant addition F_W(U₁,U₂)∈R[[U₁,U₂]], formal negation i_W(T)∈R[[T]], and unit invariant differential ω_W(T)∈1+TR[[T]]. Over any characteristic-zero field K, log_W(T)=∫₀^T ω_W(s) ds satisfies log_W(F_W(U₁,U₂))=log_W(U₁)+log_W(U₂) and log_W(i_W(T))=−log_W(T), with inverse exponential matching −x(z)/y(z) on short models; specializing the universal coefficient ring Z=ℤ[A₁,A₂,A₃,A₄,A₆]⊂Frac(Z) makes F_W a commutative formal group law with inverse i_W over every commutative ring R; in particular, whenever a subring R⊆K (such as the closed unit ball of an ultrametric field K, including y²=x³−(g₂/4)x−g₃/4 when |g₂|≤1, |g₃|≤1, and |2|=1) contains the coefficients of W, F_W, i_W, every integer multiplication series [n]_W(T), and [1/2]_W(T) when 2∈Rˣ have coefficients in R and match addition, negation, and scalar multiplication under log_W.",
      "definitions": [
        "contractive local Weierstrass series w_W(T)=T³w_U(T)",
        "regularized coordinate series A(T)=x_S(T)=w_U(T)⁻¹",
        "formal negation series i_W(T) and invariant differential ω_W(T)",
        "division-free secant slope λ(U₁,U₂) and Vieta third abscissa u₃",
        "Weierstrass formal group law F_W(U₁,U₂) and formal logarithm log_W(T)"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "normalization-weierstrass-fixed-point",
        "normalization-weierstrass-secant-addition",
        "normalization-weierstrass-logarithm-homomorphism"
